539
00:47:26.847 --> 00:47:29.224
about surviving?

540
00:47:29.641 --> 00:47:31.810
And it was like
a for-real witch?

541
00:47:32.603 --> 00:47:35.480
I think it was a for-real witch.

542
00:47:37.065 --> 00:47:38.066
I mean...

543
00:47:39.109 --> 00:47:40.485
Yeah, I think
that's what she said.

544
00:47:41.945 --> 00:47:43.864
That's like the only thing
I can remember.

545
00:47:45.532 --> 00:47:46.575
Well...

546
00:47:47.451 --> 00:47:50.162
The good news is that I think
this means there's a way out.

547
00:47:52.372 --> 00:47:53.498
What's that?

548
00:47:56.168 --> 00:47:57.753
"Survive the night."

549
00:47:57.836 --> 00:48:00.589
Right? So, maybe
if we can make it until dawn,

550
00:48:00.672 --> 00:48:02.466
then maybe this will be over.

551
00:48:02.549 --> 00:48:04.259
Okay, but what about the rest?

552
00:48:04.760 --> 00:48:06.637
"Or become a part of it."

553
00:48:07.137 --> 00:48:09.181
Yeah, part of the night, right?

554
00:48:09.264 --> 00:48:10.974
It means that
if we don't get out,

555
00:48:11.058 --> 00:48:12.226
we're stuck here forever.

556
00:48:12.309 --> 00:48:17.231
And shit like this and that
will just keep happening.

557
00:48:17.731 --> 00:48:19.691
We're turning
into something else.

558
00:48:20.567 --> 00:48:22.069
You guys get that, right?

559
00:48:22.444 --> 00:48:25.113
Okay, so we'll just
stick it out in here

560
00:48:25.197 --> 00:48:27.032
until the sun comes up,
like Max said.

561
00:48:27.741 --> 00:48:28.909
But what about Mel?

562
00:48:29.660 --> 00:48:31.578
She's still stuck here
too somewhere.

563
00:48:31.662 --> 00:48:33.705
If Mel was still stuck,
then she would be here.

564
00:48:33.789 --> 00:48:35.290
And all those people
on that wall,

565
00:48:35.374 --> 00:48:37.709
they would be here,
and they're not, so...

566
00:48:38.919 --> 00:48:40.629
- Where are they?
- Oh, my God.

567
00:48:41.129 --> 00:48:43.966
We didn't come here
looking for Mel, okay, Clover?

568
00:48:44.049 --> 00:48:46.301
We came hoping
to find you again.

569
00:48:47.010 --> 00:48:48.262
Like, the old you.

570
00:48:48.345 --> 00:48:50.556
We were hoping this
would help you move on.

571
00:48:51.056 --> 00:48:53.183
Help you get back to,
you know, living.

572
00:48:57.938 --> 00:48:59.022
Abe.

573
00:48:59.565 --> 00:49:01.316
- Are you okay?
- Here, take some.

574
00:49:03.110 --> 00:49:04.111
Abe.

575
00:49:08.156 --> 00:49:09.408
Holy fuck!

576
00:49:13.328 --> 00:49:14.913
Oh, my God! Oh, my God!

577
00:49:15.289 --> 00:49:17.708
It's in my mouth!
It's in my mouth!

578
00:49:19.001 --> 00:49:20.586
Nina! Stop! The water.

579
00:49:21.712 --> 00:49:24.112
- You saw him drink the water.
- Didn't we all drink the wat...?

580
00:49:27.342 --> 00:49:29.052
Oh, my God! Oh, my God!

581
00:49:38.437 --> 00:49:39.771
- What do we do?
- I don't know.

582
00:49:39.855 --> 00:49:41.732
I need a second to think.
That was a lot.

583
00:49:44.860 --> 00:49:45.861
Meg?

584
00:49:46.445 --> 00:49:47.446
No.

585
00:49:48.197 --> 00:49:49.198
Meg?

586
00:49:49.281 --> 00:49:51.200
- Megan?
- No, no, no. Please.

587
00:49:51.283 --> 00:49:52.492
Please. No.

588
00:49:55.037 --> 00:49:56.121
Megan.

589
00:50:02.461 --> 00:50:04.087
- What do we do, Max?
- I don't know.

590
00:50:17.851 --> 00:50:18.977
Oh, my God.

591
00:50:22.523 --> 00:50:23.899
I don't know what to do.

592
00:50:23.982 --> 00:50:24.983
Help me.

593
00:50:25.067 --> 00:50:26.860
Megan. What do we do?

594
00:50:27.611 --> 00:50:28.612
Megan.

595
00:50:35.118 --> 00:50:36.119
Kill me, Max.

596
00:50:37.162 --> 00:50:39.039
What? No!

597
00:50:39.122 --> 00:50:41.124
Please.
All of our friends are dead.

598
00:50:41.208 --> 00:50:42.501
And we drank the water,

599
00:50:42.584 --> 00:50:44.229
and we're covered
in the same shit they were.

600
00:50:44.253 --> 00:50:47.464
No, we need to start over
and come up with a plan.

601
00:50:47.548 --> 00:50:49.675
Look. The sand
has almost run out.

602
00:50:49.758 --> 00:50:52.803
It's almost dawn.
Okay? And maybe we'll survive.

603
00:50:52.886 --> 00:50:56.473
We'll come back. Okay? Okay?
It's only been twice so far.

604
00:50:56.557 --> 00:50:58.350
And you saw the other signatures
in the book.

605
00:50:58.433 --> 00:50:59.810
Everyone else has way more.

606
00:51:00.686 --> 00:51:01.895
We'll come back.

607
00:51:02.312 --> 00:51:04.064
We need to try and save them.

608
00:51:10.988 --> 00:51:14.783
Please do it. Please hurry.
Max, hurry.

609
00:51:19.037 --> 00:51:20.247
I can't! I can't.

610
00:51:20.330 --> 00:51:21.331
Max, no.

611
00:51:21.415 --> 00:51:22.958
I can't. I'm sorry.

612
00:51:58.577 --> 00:51:59.745
You?

613
00:52:02.164 --> 00:52:04.499
You almost made it.

614
00:52:04.583 --> 00:52:05.959
Almost!

615
00:52:06.251 --> 00:52:08.462
But not quite.

616
00:52:08.545 --> 00:52:13.884
You don't survive
by sitting still, Miss Clover.

617
00:52:18.263 --> 00:52:19.389
What?

618
00:52:56.844 --> 00:52:58.303
Is anyone else
growing new teeth?

619
00:52:59.096 --> 00:53:00.764
Wait, how many
are we supposed to have?

620
00:53:00.848 --> 00:53:02.328
I don't know,
but it's an even number.

621
00:53:04.476 --> 00:53:07.980
Guys, clearly it doesn't work
to just wait it out.

622
00:53:08.063 --> 00:53:09.064
I mean, there has to be

623
00:53:09.147 --> 00:53:10.947
something here
to help us come up with a plan.

624
00:53:20.409 --> 00:53:22.494
Holy fuck. This is the guy.

625
00:53:22.953 --> 00:53:26.373
This is... Yeah, this is the guy
from the gas station. Look!

626
00:53:26.456 --> 00:53:28.083
- What?
- He's Dr Alan Hill.

627
00:53:28.834 --> 00:53:31.170
He's, like, somehow
connected to this place.

628
00:53:31.253 --> 00:53:33.088
Why? What's so special about it?

629
00:53:33.172 --> 00:53:35.465
Twenty years ago
there was a mining disaster.

630
00:53:35.549 --> 00:53:37.259
Happened right here
in Glore Valley.

631
00:53:40.012 --> 00:53:41.471
"Working with outside engineers,

632
00:53:41.555 --> 00:53:42.866
"investigators confirmed
the destruction

633
00:53:42.890 --> 00:53:44.576
"was caused by boring
too deep into the earth

634
00:53:44.600 --> 00:53:45.976
"and too far under the town,

635
00:53:46.059 --> 00:53:48.187
"resulting in the death
of over 1,100 people.

636
00:53:48.270 --> 00:53:50.355
"Dr Alan Hill,
a trauma specialist,"

637
00:53:50.439 --> 00:53:52.733
"was brought in
to work with the survivors."

638
00:53:53.859 --> 00:53:56.528
The whole town got, like,
swallowed up by the earth.

639
00:53:59.531 --> 00:54:01.783
That's why there's
no other houses here.

640
00:54:01.867 --> 00:54:03.619
And that's why
there's windows down here.

641
00:54:04.119 --> 00:54:05.787
This whole floor
used to be above ground.

642
00:54:07.539 --> 00:54:08.819
That means
that's the front door.

643
00:54:08.957 --> 00:54:10.417
Guys, who gives a shit?

644
00:54:10.501 --> 00:54:11.541
I feel like we really need

645
00:54:11.585 --> 00:54:12.687
to just be getting
weapons right now.

646
00:54:12.711 --> 00:54:14.296
Okay, but I think we need more

647
00:54:14.379 --> 00:54:15.659
than just weapons
of brute force.

648
00:54:15.714 --> 00:54:16.715
Like what, Max?

649
00:54:31.355 --> 00:54:32.356
No, thank you.

650
00:54:32.814 --> 00:54:34.608
I think we need the Bible
as a weapon.

651
00:54:34.691 --> 00:54:36.902
Yeah, dude, not against
a masked maniac, though.

652
00:54:36.985 --> 00:54:38.625
But we're not just up
against that psycho.

653
00:54:39.029 --> 00:54:40.965
Every single night something new
is trying to kill us.

654
00:54:40.989 --> 00:54:42.491
Yeah, but why?

655
00:54:43.951 --> 00:54:45.077
Think about it.

656
00:54:45.160 --> 00:54:47.538
If it was the same thing
over and over again,

657
00:54:47.621 --> 00:54:49.456
you'd become
less scared over time.

658
00:54:50.707 --> 00:54:54.086
But what's more terrifying than
not knowing what comes next.

659
00:54:54.837 --> 00:54:55.838
Whoever,

660
00:54:56.421 --> 00:54:57.631
whatever,

661
00:54:57.714 --> 00:54:58.924
is doing this...

662
00:55:00.050 --> 00:55:01.343
it wants to keep us afraid.

663
00:55:01.426 --> 00:55:02.803
Yeah, well, it's working.

664
00:55:04.638 --> 00:55:05.848
I think I found something.

665
00:55:05.931 --> 00:55:08.016
I don't think that's gonna
help us. A VHS tape?

666
00:55:08.100 --> 00:55:09.560
Knowledge is power.

667
00:55:16.108 --> 00:55:17.526
Great, that's exactly
what we need

668
00:55:17.609 --> 00:55:18.610
- right now.
- Wow.

669
00:55:19.111 --> 00:55:20.112
Sorry, sorry, sorry.

670
00:55:20.195 --> 00:55:21.488
Very powerful, Max. Thank you.

671
00:55:21.572 --> 00:55:22.882
Just give me a second.
I have another one.

672
00:55:22.906 --> 00:55:24.992
Do you want us
to leave you alone for a second?

673
00:55:25.075 --> 00:55:26.715
- Just shut up. Abe.
- All right, all right.

674
00:55:55.939 --> 00:55:56.982
Please.

675
00:55:58.233 --> 00:56:01.528
What are you doing to me?
Why do I keep coming back?

676
00:56:03.530 --> 00:56:06.491
Why do you have these things
that keep killing me?

677
00:56:07.159 --> 00:56:08.202
Who are you?!

678
00:56:08.785 --> 00:56:10.913
What do you want from me?! Huh?

679
00:56:14.041 --> 00:56:18.670
The patient showed signs of
starvation and muscle atrophy.

680
00:56:18.754 --> 00:56:19.838
What's happening to me?

681
00:56:19.922 --> 00:56:24.176
But most importantly,
intense fear, anxiety,

682
00:56:24.259 --> 00:56:27.596
feelings of hopelessness
and utter despair.

683
00:56:28.722 --> 00:56:32.017
Fortunately for my experiments,

684
00:56:32.100 --> 00:56:35.562
the trauma of the mining
disaster still lingers,

685
00:56:35.646 --> 00:56:39.525
affecting both survivors
and visitors.

686
00:56:44.404 --> 00:56:46.240
The longer he was trapped here,

687
00:56:46.323 --> 00:56:49.409
the more desperate
and afraid he became...

688
00:56:49.493 --> 00:56:52.287
and also the more monstrous.

689
00:56:56.166 --> 00:56:57.376
Help! God, please!

690
00:56:57.459 --> 00:57:02.339
Eleven nights. That's the most
in my experiments so far.

691
00:57:07.970 --> 00:57:11.306
Soon, those emotions
began to affect his body

692
00:57:11.390 --> 00:57:13.767
in more interesting ways,

693
00:57:15.435 --> 00:57:18.480
transforming into
a creature known

694
00:57:18.564 --> 00:57:20.399
as the Wendigo.

695
00:57:20.482 --> 00:57:23.402
It is no coincidence
that in psychology,

696
00:57:23.485 --> 00:57:26.572
the Wendigo represents
extreme hunger,

697
00:57:26.655 --> 00:57:29.074
extreme want.

698
00:57:35.747 --> 00:57:37.249
That's what's happening to us.

699
00:57:38.166 --> 00:57:39.251
That's what we're becoming.

700
00:57:39.835 --> 00:57:40.919
Yeah.

701
00:57:42.337 --> 00:57:44.089
Now you're getting it.

702
00:57:47.843 --> 00:57:49.178
Let us out.

703
00:57:53.807 --> 00:57:55.142
Let us out!

704
00:57:55.225 --> 00:57:57.644
Oh, there's a way out,

705
00:57:57.728 --> 00:58:00.189
but not without a price.

706
00:58:01.481 --> 00:58:03.192
- Ask him how.
- Abe!

707
00:58:04.109 --> 00:58:05.110
How?

708
00:58:05.194 --> 00:58:08.197
Someone always has to die.

709
00:58:08.280 --> 00:58:12.201
Four of you can leave,
but one has to die.

710
00:58:12.284 --> 00:58:13.493
No.

711
00:58:13.827 --> 00:58:14.828
Nice try, asshole.

712
00:58:14.912 --> 00:58:17.140
Wait, hold on. I think we should
at least just hear him out.

713
00:58:17.164 --> 00:58:20.083
Why? Are you willing
to sacrifice yourself for us?

714
00:58:22.419 --> 00:58:23.504
No.

715
00:58:23.587 --> 00:58:24.880
We can't trust this guy.

716
00:58:24.963 --> 00:58:26.298
Which means our only real shot

717
00:58:26.381 --> 00:58:27.984
of getting out
of here is getting some answers,

718
00:58:28.008 --> 00:58:29.593
and the one
with the answers is Hill.

719
00:58:30.761 --> 00:58:33.263
He's here somewhere.
I can feel it.

720
00:59:04.294 --> 00:59:07.506
How is this supposed to help us?
The whole town was destroyed.

721
00:59:07.589 --> 00:59:08.674
He could be anywhere.

722
00:59:11.593 --> 00:59:12.719
No. Not "anywhere."

723
00:59:17.307 --> 00:59:18.308
He's there.

724
00:59:18.392 --> 00:59:19.536
Was there. And Nina just said

725
00:59:19.560 --> 00:59:20.936
none of this even
exists any more.

726
00:59:21.019 --> 00:59:23.438
So we just need to try
to get him out of hiding.

727
00:59:24.857 --> 00:59:26.400
I wanna see you. Face-to-face.

728
00:59:26.483 --> 00:59:28.110
Clover, what are you doing?

729
00:59:28.485 --> 00:59:30.112
He's the key to all of this.

730
00:59:30.195 --> 00:59:31.822
That can be arranged.

731
00:59:32.447 --> 00:59:35.409
But just you, Clover.
Not your friends.

732
00:59:35.492 --> 00:59:36.785
- No.
- Clover, no.

733
00:59:36.869 --> 00:59:39.162
This is a trap,
just like everything else here.

734
00:59:39.246 --> 00:59:40.515
Actually, I think
it's a pretty good idea.

735
00:59:40.539 --> 00:59:42.124
Abe, just shut
the fuck up, okay?

736
00:59:42.207 --> 00:59:43.458
It's only night four. Clover,

737
00:59:43.542 --> 00:59:45.353
- you're gonna have more chances.
- We don't know that.

738
00:59:45.377 --> 00:59:47.355
All the other signatures
in the book go way past that.

739
00:59:47.379 --> 00:59:48.881
Guys, Abe is right.

740
00:59:49.882 --> 00:59:52.342
- This is our chance.
- No. Don't listen to him.

741
00:59:52.426 --> 00:59:54.219
I'm out in the woods.

742
00:59:54.303 --> 00:59:56.471
I'm here with your sister.

743
00:59:57.890 --> 00:59:59.850
I might just let you see her.

744
01:00:00.142 --> 01:00:01.768
- Clo.
- There you go. Yeah.

745
01:00:01.852 --> 01:00:03.437
- Clover, come on.
- No.

746
01:00:04.354 --> 01:00:05.606
I have to try.

747
01:00:05.689 --> 01:00:07.232
- No, no, no. Clover!
- Let her go!

748
01:00:07.316 --> 01:00:08.984
- Back off!
- Let her go, let her go!

749
01:00:09.067 --> 01:00:11.820
- What is wrong with you?
- What? Hey!

750
01:00:11.904 --> 01:00:13.697
Hey! Nina!

751
01:00:16.950 --> 01:00:18.118
You fucking prick!

752
01:00:18.202 --> 01:00:20.180
What?! I didn't think
she was gonna actually do it.

753
01:00:20.204 --> 01:00:21.622
Yes, you did. You knew she would

754
01:00:21.705 --> 01:00:23.457
and you took advantage.
Fucking coward!

755
01:00:23.540 --> 01:00:25.042
Look, Megan,
we need to find Clover

756
01:00:25.125 --> 01:00:26.186
before something
permanent happens.

757
01:00:26.210 --> 01:00:27.812
- To do what?
- We're gonna go and find her.

758
01:00:27.836 --> 01:00:29.046
And if she's dead already,

759
01:00:29.129 --> 01:00:32.925
we're gonna kill each other
and start over again.

760
01:00:33.008 --> 01:00:34.134
Sounds like a plan.

761
01:00:34.218 --> 01:00:35.219
Abe first.

762
01:00:35.302 --> 01:00:37.262
Wait-Wait! Just wait, hold on.

763
01:00:37.346 --> 01:00:38.889
Say we start over.

764
01:00:38.972 --> 01:00:40.182
What then?

765
01:00:41.016 --> 01:00:43.268
We just keep running away
until we run out of chances?

766
01:00:43.352 --> 01:00:44.561
Are you fucking serious?

767
01:00:44.645 --> 01:00:46.122
I don't wanna live
knowing that I'm alive

768
01:00:46.146 --> 01:00:47.648
because someone else is dead!

769
01:00:47.731 --> 01:00:49.733
- Because Clover is dead!
- But look at us!

770
01:00:49.816 --> 01:00:52.528
How many more deaths
do you have in you? Be honest.

771
01:00:53.153 --> 01:00:55.906
I mean, didn't she try and kill
herself twice last year?

772
01:00:56.198 --> 01:00:58.534
Isn't this just giving her
what she wa...?

773
01:01:06.291 --> 01:01:08.043
What the fuck, Nina?!

774
01:01:08.669 --> 01:01:09.962
You guys go find Clover.

775
01:01:10.629 --> 01:01:12.607
Otherwise it'll be two people
we have to leave behind.

776
01:01:12.631 --> 01:01:13.674
Let's go.

777
01:01:23.141 --> 01:01:24.935
You better hope they find her.

778
01:01:30.774 --> 01:01:31.900
I'm here!

779
01:01:32.943 --> 01:01:33.986
You have me.

780
01:01:43.912 --> 01:01:45.038
No.

781
01:01:58.552 --> 01:01:59.678
Oh, no.

782
01:02:00.179 --> 01:02:03.807
No, please, please, please.
Please! Sh... Please.

783
01:02:04.474 --> 01:02:05.893
No, no. No!

784
01:02:05.976 --> 01:02:09.730
Please! Please! Please! Please!

785
01:02:09.813 --> 01:02:10.814
Please!

786
01:02:11.773 --> 01:02:14.693
No! Wait, wait!
Oh, my God.

787
01:02:25.454 --> 01:02:27.581
You need to try
and survive, Nina.

788
01:02:29.333 --> 01:02:30.626
I will.

789
01:02:31.793 --> 01:02:33.128
Just not this time.

790
01:02:48.685 --> 01:02:50.854
I'm scared of dying, Nina.

791
01:02:51.647 --> 01:02:53.148
Like, really dying.

792
01:02:54.316 --> 01:02:55.526
Me too.

793
01:02:57.528 --> 01:03:00.322
But living without my friends
scares me even more.

794
01:03:05.202 --> 01:03:06.495
Him first.

795
01:03:06.912 --> 01:03:07.913
What?

796
01:03:14.378 --> 01:03:15.546
Clover!

797
01:03:16.046 --> 01:03:17.172
Clo!

798
01:03:28.934 --> 01:03:30.477
Holy shit.

799
01:03:43.824 --> 01:03:44.867
Clover?

800
01:03:46.034 --> 01:03:47.286
Clover!

801
01:03:49.663 --> 01:03:50.914
Clover!

802
01:04:01.258 --> 01:04:02.426
Over there.

803
01:04:10.100 --> 01:04:11.185
The hell?

804
01:04:13.103 --> 01:04:14.271
Run!

805
01:04:22.821 --> 01:04:24.448
Max! Max!

806
01:04:29.912 --> 01:04:31.079
It'll break if I move.

807
01:04:33.957 --> 01:04:35.626
Okay, okay.
Just give me your hand.

808
01:04:38.837 --> 01:04:42.007
Okay, okay, I got you.
I'm gonna pull on three. Okay?

809
01:04:43.175 --> 01:04:44.176
Okay.

810
01:04:44.259 --> 01:04:45.969
One, two, three.

811
01:04:51.975 --> 01:04:52.976
Meg!

812
01:04:53.685 --> 01:04:54.686
Meg!

813
01:05:33.225 --> 01:05:34.726
Clover! Clover!

814
01:05:34.810 --> 01:05:35.811
Max!

815
01:05:35.894 --> 01:05:37.437
You're here.

816
01:05:37.521 --> 01:05:40.190
I got you. I got you.
Okay. Ready?

817
01:05:42.109 --> 01:05:43.110
Okay.

818
01:05:45.362 --> 01:05:47.364
I'm sorry. Aw, fuck.

819
01:05:50.117 --> 01:05:51.368
Max. Max. Max.

820
01:05:56.874 --> 01:05:57.875
Is that Melanie?

821
01:06:10.470 --> 01:06:12.973
- Come on. Come on.
- Melanie! No, no!

822
01:06:19.229 --> 01:06:20.355
I got you. I got you.

823
01:06:34.912 --> 01:06:35.913
Melanie!

824
01:06:42.085 --> 01:06:43.712
I fucked up, Max.

825
01:06:44.713 --> 01:06:45.714
What?

826
01:06:45.797 --> 01:06:47.007
- I fucked up.
- No.

827
01:06:47.090 --> 01:06:48.759
- Yes. Yes. Yes.
- No, no, no.

828
01:06:49.426 --> 01:06:50.427
Yeah.

829
01:06:52.763 --> 01:06:54.556
Why did you come for me?

830
01:06:55.891 --> 01:06:56.971
You all could have escaped.

831
01:06:57.684 --> 01:07:00.729
No. No, no, no. We'll have
more chances to get out of this.

832
01:07:01.647 --> 01:07:03.273
Okay? Together.

833
01:07:05.234 --> 01:07:07.152
I'm not leaving you behind.

834
01:07:15.619 --> 01:07:16.787
When we die, like...

835
01:07:17.913 --> 01:07:19.081
for real...

836
01:07:20.332 --> 01:07:22.459
you think we get the chance
to do it all again?

837
01:07:25.295 --> 01:07:26.588
I hope not.

838
01:07:27.673 --> 01:07:28.715
Why?

839
01:07:31.718 --> 01:07:33.762
Just means more somehow

840
01:07:34.555 --> 01:07:36.306
when you know
you only have one shot.

841
01:07:40.102 --> 01:07:41.103
Yeah.

842
01:07:45.607 --> 01:07:47.317
Are the others still alive?

843
01:07:48.068 --> 01:07:50.112
I'm not sure about Abe and Nina.

844
01:07:50.195 --> 01:07:51.196
What about Megan?

845
01:07:59.663 --> 01:08:01.683
What are you doing? I just said
I don't know about Abe and Nina.

846
01:08:01.707 --> 01:08:02.958
But we know that Megan is dead.

847
01:08:03.041 --> 01:08:05.294
That's enough
for me to try and start again.

848
01:08:08.172 --> 01:08:10.048
This next one might be our last.

849
01:08:12.217 --> 01:08:14.178
But I think
we can all survive, Max.

850
01:08:14.261 --> 01:08:17.471
So let's get started
by dying first.

851
01:08:17.555 --> 01:08:20.475
I know. I know. It's okay.

852
01:08:25.397 --> 01:08:26.398
Yeah.

853
01:08:32.362 --> 01:08:33.363
Thank you.

854
01:09:05.437 --> 01:09:06.438
Hey!

855
01:09:07.648 --> 01:09:08.774
Fuck y...!

856
01:09:19.993 --> 01:09:21.453
Just one second, Mel.

857
01:09:27.542 --> 01:09:29.586
Mel. Mel.

858
01:09:30.962 --> 01:09:33.215
Wait, hey. You should take this.

859
01:09:33.298 --> 01:09:34.299
No, Clover.

860
01:09:34.383 --> 01:09:35.610
It was Mom's.
You should take it.

861
01:09:35.634 --> 01:09:37.803
No. You keep it.

862
01:09:39.720 --> 01:09:41.449
Well, do you wanna
wait out the storm at least?

863
01:09:41.473 --> 01:09:44.852
I just wanna get going.
It's a long way to New York.

864
01:09:46.478 --> 01:09:48.063
But then it's just me.

865
01:09:48.564 --> 01:09:49.689
Yeah.

866
01:09:49.773 --> 01:09:53.026
I mean, I've asked you to come
with me how many times now?

867
01:09:53.777 --> 01:09:54.778
Let's just leave.

868
01:09:55.445 --> 01:09:57.281
I told you that I can't.

869
01:09:57.364 --> 01:09:59.616
You can't sit still
for the rest of your life, Clo.

870
01:10:00.284 --> 01:10:01.285
It's not living.

871
01:10:02.035 --> 01:10:03.235
At least I'm not running away.

872
01:10:03.787 --> 01:10:05.587
You think that's what I'm doing,
running away?

873
01:10:05.622 --> 01:10:07.058
I'm actually running
towards something.

874
01:10:07.082 --> 01:10:08.250
Towards what?

875
01:10:08.333 --> 01:10:11.837
School. A new city. A new life.

876
01:10:11.920 --> 01:10:12.921
I love you.

877
01:10:14.256 --> 01:10:15.883
But I can't just sit here

878
01:10:15.966 --> 01:10:18.051
and waste away
becoming something I'd hate.

879
01:10:28.729 --> 01:10:29.730
Mel.

880
01:10:30.731 --> 01:10:32.232
Mel, wait!

881
01:10:38.071 --> 01:10:40.240
Hey. Hey.
Hey, hey, hey. Hey.

882
01:10:46.455 --> 01:10:48.207
I had to drag you in here.

883
01:10:49.249 --> 01:10:50.542
I thought we lost you.

884
01:10:51.877 --> 01:10:52.878
Hey.

885
01:10:52.961 --> 01:10:54.129
Is there...?

886
01:10:55.005 --> 01:10:56.423
Is there something on my back?

887
01:11:02.471 --> 01:11:04.223
- You look fine.
- Are you sure?

888
01:11:05.057 --> 01:11:06.808
It feels like there's
something back there.

889
01:11:16.902 --> 01:11:18.445
How long have we been here?

890
01:11:20.113 --> 01:11:23.492
I don't know.
Three or four nights, I think.

891
01:11:24.076 --> 01:11:25.160
Five, actually.

892
01:11:25.869 --> 01:11:26.870
It's been five.

893
01:11:26.954 --> 01:11:28.121
No, not five.

894
01:11:29.164 --> 01:11:30.999
- Thirteen.
- What?

895
01:11:31.083 --> 01:11:32.584
It's been 13 nights.

896
01:11:34.127 --> 01:11:35.420
Go check the book.

897
01:11:54.982 --> 01:11:56.441
Yeah, nobody has more than 13.

898
01:11:59.945 --> 01:12:01.321
Tonight might be
our last chance.

899
01:12:16.086 --> 01:12:18.297
I don't remember
any of these things.

900
01:12:19.673 --> 01:12:21.175
Yeah, me neither.

901
01:12:22.134 --> 01:12:23.802
We didn't do what we said, Max.

902
01:12:25.012 --> 01:12:27.598
The next one wasn't the last and
neither was the one after that,

903
01:12:27.681 --> 01:12:29.016
or the one after that.

904
01:12:37.900 --> 01:12:38.984
Wait.

905
01:12:40.485 --> 01:12:41.486
Where's Megan?

906
01:12:45.324 --> 01:12:46.658
Shit. Megan.

907
01:12:52.331 --> 01:12:53.832
She's not in there.

908
01:12:53.916 --> 01:12:55.476
Maybe something
already happened to her?

909
01:12:55.542 --> 01:12:57.419
Or it got to her first.

910
01:12:57.503 --> 01:12:58.587
What? What got to her?

911
01:12:59.296 --> 01:13:00.506
The night.

912
01:13:02.508 --> 01:13:05.719
Survive the night
or become a part of it.

913
01:13:06.595 --> 01:13:07.864
There's nothing that says
it would happen

914
01:13:07.888 --> 01:13:08.948
to all of us at the same time.

915
01:13:08.972 --> 01:13:11.141
Because there's nothing
that says anything, Abe.

916
01:13:11.225 --> 01:13:12.368
I know, but different people
could have

917
01:13:12.392 --> 01:13:13.453
a different number of chances,

918
01:13:13.477 --> 01:13:14.478
like it's random.

919
01:13:15.187 --> 01:13:16.188
You could be right.

920
01:13:17.189 --> 01:13:20.609
Okay. Okay, great.
So then what do we do, huh?

921
01:13:21.109 --> 01:13:22.861
Megan is just... She's gone?

922
01:13:23.695 --> 01:13:26.323
Fuck. Why can't we
remember anything?

923
01:13:26.406 --> 01:13:27.908
Why didn't we write
anything down?

924
01:13:27.991 --> 01:13:29.284
Would it have mattered?

925
01:13:29.368 --> 01:13:31.208
It'd be gone once
the night starts over anyway.

926
01:13:31.286 --> 01:13:34.122
- Your signature isn't.
- But that's all that's in there.

927
01:13:34.873 --> 01:13:36.291
Didn't I record something?

928
01:13:40.963 --> 01:13:42.297
Holy shit. Guys, come here.

929
01:13:49.263 --> 01:13:50.264
Look.

930
01:13:51.098 --> 01:13:52.432
There's so much stuff.

931
01:13:53.767 --> 01:13:54.852
What?

932
01:13:54.935 --> 01:13:56.436
Okay. All right.

933
01:13:58.397 --> 01:14:00.190
Don't worry. We'll get it.

934
01:14:00.274 --> 01:14:01.275
Okay.

935
01:14:01.358 --> 01:14:02.502
Just don't move.
I'm gonna grab it.

936
01:14:02.526 --> 01:14:03.569
- Oh, my God.
- Okay.

937
01:14:03.652 --> 01:14:06.029
Abe? Abe, be careful.

938
01:14:06.113 --> 01:14:07.573
- Please get it.
- Abe?

939
01:14:08.323 --> 01:14:09.366
What?

940
01:14:09.950 --> 01:14:11.535
Is it gone?

941
01:14:12.452 --> 01:14:13.453
Is it gone?

942
01:14:14.746 --> 01:14:16.123
Yeah. It's gone.

943
01:14:16.707 --> 01:14:18.041
Did it fall off?

944
01:14:20.544 --> 01:14:21.753
- What the fuck?!
- What?

945
01:14:22.254 --> 01:14:23.654
- Holy shit.
- Is it still on my face?

946
01:14:25.549 --> 01:14:28.343
- It's fine, it's fine.
- Clover, it's okay, it's okay.

947
01:14:28.886 --> 01:14:30.387
Is it still on my face?!

948
01:14:30.470 --> 01:14:31.471
Oh, my God.

949
01:14:37.603 --> 01:14:39.188
Fuck. It's locked.

950
01:14:39.271 --> 01:14:40.397
Fuck.

951
01:14:40.480 --> 01:14:41.481
What's that?

952
01:14:42.774 --> 01:14:45.402
What the fuck?
What the fuck is that?

953
01:14:45.485 --> 01:14:46.528
Is that a person?

954
01:14:46.612 --> 01:14:48.822
Holy shit, holy shit.
What the fuck?!

955
01:14:50.824 --> 01:14:52.576
Max. We should turn back.

956
01:15:01.460 --> 01:15:02.544
Look at all this shit.

957
01:15:03.712 --> 01:15:05.064
There's fucking blood
on the walls.

958
01:15:05.088 --> 01:15:06.131
Just be quiet, Abe.

959
01:15:10.552 --> 01:15:11.762
What the hell?

960
01:15:15.057 --> 01:15:16.058
Max!

961
01:15:17.809 --> 01:15:18.894
Abe!

962
01:15:19.353 --> 01:15:20.979
Die! Die! Die!

963
01:15:21.063 --> 01:15:22.064
Max!

964
01:15:22.856 --> 01:15:24.650
Die! Die!

965
01:15:26.944 --> 01:15:29.279
Why won't you fucking die?!

966
01:15:33.325 --> 01:15:34.952
Oh, shit. What the fuck?

967
01:15:36.078 --> 01:15:38.121
- What is that?
- What the fuck is that?

968
01:15:38.205 --> 01:15:39.206
What is that?!

969
01:15:39.998 --> 01:15:41.458
- Nina!
- What the fuck?! No!

970
01:15:42.042 --> 01:15:43.502
- Nina!
- What is that?!

971
01:15:43.585 --> 01:15:45.462
Abe! What is that?!

972
01:15:45.546 --> 01:15:46.588
Holy shit!

973
01:16:36.513 --> 01:16:37.973
I'm gonna follow him

974
01:16:38.056 --> 01:16:40.809
and see if I can find out
anything that will help us.

975
01:16:41.435 --> 01:16:42.436
I have to try.

976
01:17:06.168 --> 01:17:07.544
- Fuck.
- Oh, my God. They're coming.

977
01:17:09.213 --> 01:17:10.589
Fuck. They're all coming.

978
01:17:12.132 --> 01:17:13.133
We need to run.

979
01:17:13.217 --> 01:17:15.302
All we've been doing
is running away.

980
01:17:15.385 --> 01:17:17.471
So let's start running
towards something.

981
01:17:17.554 --> 01:17:18.680
What do you mean?

982
01:17:24.978 --> 01:17:26.058
I'm going into that tunnel.

983
01:17:26.104 --> 01:17:28.315
Clover. We don't even know
what's over there.

984
01:17:28.398 --> 01:17:29.709
You realise this could
be our last night.

985
01:17:29.733 --> 01:17:30.734
Good.

986
01:17:32.277 --> 01:17:34.112
It means more
when you only have one shot.

987
01:17:35.531 --> 01:17:37.199
I'm sorry I got you into this.

988
01:17:38.492 --> 01:17:39.868
You're all here because of me.

989
01:17:41.662 --> 01:17:44.039
Melanie was my family,
but you're my family too.

990
01:17:44.122 --> 01:17:46.667
So I'm gonna save Megan,
kill Hill

991
01:17:46.750 --> 01:17:48.544
and then get us
the fuck out of here.

992
01:17:50.879 --> 01:17:51.964
I'm done with death.

993
01:18:08.397 --> 01:18:09.439
Clover.

994
01:18:13.652 --> 01:18:14.820
We stick together.

995
01:18:25.873 --> 01:18:27.875
Oh, fuck.

996
01:18:29.751 --> 01:18:30.752
Come on.

997
01:18:31.837 --> 01:18:33.255
Oh, my God.

998
01:18:51.565 --> 01:18:52.900
Holy shit.

999
01:18:53.567 --> 01:18:54.860
This place is huge.

1000
01:19:13.587 --> 01:19:14.588
Hey, careful.

1001
01:19:28.393 --> 01:19:29.436
Watch your step.

1002
01:19:39.446 --> 01:19:40.489
Come on.

1003
01:20:31.832 --> 01:20:32.833
Is that...?

1004
01:20:39.756 --> 01:20:41.091
Don't move.

1005
01:21:02.571 --> 01:21:03.906
Go, go, go!

1006
01:21:03.989 --> 01:21:06.283
Go! Go, go, go!

1007
01:21:06.366 --> 01:21:08.076
Go! Go, go, go!

1008
01:21:13.373 --> 01:21:15.834
- Nina! Nina! Go! Come on!
- Go, go, go!

1009
01:21:17.002 --> 01:21:18.212
Come on, guys!

1010
01:21:44.154 --> 01:21:46.240
Go, go, go! Go!

1011
01:21:47.032 --> 01:21:49.701
Guys, right here, right here!
Right here!

1012
01:21:50.577 --> 01:21:52.120
Go! Go, go!

1013
01:21:58.585 --> 01:22:00.045
Wait! Wait! Wait!

1014
01:22:02.256 --> 01:22:03.382
Oh, fuck.

1015
01:22:11.014 --> 01:22:13.725
- Max. Max, Max!
- Go! We'll find another way!

1016
01:22:13.809 --> 01:22:14.852
Max, no!

1017
01:22:15.394 --> 01:22:16.603
Go! Go find Megan!

1018
01:22:17.646 --> 01:22:19.606
Go! We'll make it out of here.

1019
01:22:21.066 --> 01:22:22.109
Hey, asshole!

1020
01:22:25.737 --> 01:22:27.072
Oh, fuck.

1021
01:23:49.613 --> 01:23:50.989
Please don't do this. Mel.

1022
01:23:55.202 --> 01:23:57.287
It's m... It's me. It's me.

1023
01:24:24.898 --> 01:24:26.149
I love you, Mel.

1024
01:24:28.068 --> 01:24:30.445
But I'm getting the fuck out
of this hellhole.

1025
01:24:40.455 --> 01:24:41.540
Max!

1026
01:24:54.970 --> 01:24:55.971
Fuck.

1027
01:24:59.266 --> 01:25:01.560
Fuck you, asshole. Die!

1028
01:25:11.737 --> 01:25:12.988
Aw, fuck.

1029
01:27:29.875 --> 01:27:30.876
Help!

1030
01:27:30.959 --> 01:27:32.794
- Megan!
- Help!

1031
01:27:36.715 --> 01:27:38.133
- Megan!
- Clover!

1032
01:27:38.217 --> 01:27:39.218
Watch out!

1033
01:27:50.562 --> 01:27:52.397
Megan, I'm gonna find a way

1034
01:27:52.481 --> 01:27:53.666
out of here.
I'm gonna get a key, okay?

1035
01:27:53.690 --> 01:27:54.691
Hurry!

1036
01:28:35.065 --> 01:28:40.237
You have been
an intriguing patient, Clover.

1037
01:28:44.241 --> 01:28:46.994
Far more interesting
than the rest.

1038
01:28:48.620 --> 01:28:50.038
Severe depression,

1039
01:28:51.081 --> 01:28:54.084
two failed suicide attempts,

1040
01:28:54.168 --> 01:28:56.503
extreme anxiety...

1041
01:28:57.296 --> 01:28:59.339
You've lost control, Clover.

1042
01:28:59.423 --> 01:29:03.051
And that's evident by every
monster you've encountered here.

1043
01:29:03.969 --> 01:29:06.180
You see, they each represent

1044
01:29:06.263 --> 01:29:09.391
a unique manifestation
of your psyche.

1045
01:29:11.476 --> 01:29:12.811
What are you talking about?

1046
01:29:12.895 --> 01:29:16.231
Being chased
by a masked psycho is common.

1047
01:29:16.315 --> 01:29:18.817
Everyone feels powerless
in some way.

1048
01:29:20.027 --> 01:29:25.073
And the witch is, of course,
a personification of repression.

1049
01:29:25.157 --> 01:29:28.911
Now, the spontaneous combustion...

1050
01:29:28.994 --> 01:29:31.705
Very rare, Clover.

1051
01:29:32.956 --> 01:29:34.541
I think it's a nod

1052
01:29:34.625 --> 01:29:38.545
to your more
self-destructive tendencies.

1053
01:29:38.629 --> 01:29:39.630
Fuck you.

1054
01:29:41.048 --> 01:29:42.799
I am getting my friends
out of here.

1055
01:29:42.883 --> 01:29:45.928
Well, you're the only one
who can, Clover.

1056
01:29:47.012 --> 01:29:48.388
This place...

1057
01:29:49.806 --> 01:29:54.353
is drawing on your insecurities
and your fears.

1058
01:29:55.687 --> 01:29:58.982
I'm sorry, are you telling me
that this was all in my head?

1059
01:29:59.066 --> 01:30:00.484
Is none of this real?

1060
01:30:00.567 --> 01:30:01.944
Of course it's real.

1061
01:30:02.486 --> 01:30:06.406
But you are the engine
that makes it run,

1062
01:30:06.490 --> 01:30:08.992
just like Melanie
and all the others

1063
01:30:09.076 --> 01:30:12.412
made it run, run, run, run.

1064
01:30:20.003 --> 01:30:21.964
Help! Help!

1065
01:30:22.047 --> 01:30:23.215
You hear that, Clover?

1066
01:30:23.298 --> 01:30:26.343
Your friends
are all about to die again.

1067
01:30:26.426 --> 01:30:28.929
Tick, tick, tick...

1068
01:30:29.513 --> 01:30:31.139
Why? Why are you doing this?

1069
01:30:32.224 --> 01:30:33.267
Why?

1070
01:30:34.351 --> 01:30:37.187
Because this is what I study.

1071
01:30:37.771 --> 01:30:40.357
Fear is my trade.

1072
01:30:40.858 --> 01:30:45.571
People with trauma,
like yourself, Clover...

1073
01:30:45.654 --> 01:30:50.325
And places with trauma,
like Glore Valley...

1074
01:30:51.285 --> 01:30:53.579
When I put
the two of them together...

1075
01:30:55.789 --> 01:30:58.250
trauma becomes terror...

1076
01:30:59.168 --> 01:31:00.419
and sparks...

1077
01:31:00.961 --> 01:31:02.171
ignite.

1078
01:31:05.424 --> 01:31:07.384
Help!
Shit, guys, I'm fucking stuck!

1079
01:31:10.637 --> 01:31:11.680
And it creates...

1080
01:31:12.556 --> 01:31:13.849
the perfect...

1081
01:31:15.058 --> 01:31:16.143
horror.

1082
01:31:33.160 --> 01:31:35.662
Fuck, they're coming!
Please help! Please!

1083
01:31:40.292 --> 01:31:42.252
But to make this

1084
01:31:42.753 --> 01:31:44.546
truly effective

1085
01:31:44.630 --> 01:31:46.798
like I've said before,

1086
01:31:47.424 --> 01:31:50.260
someone always has to die.

1087
01:31:50.344 --> 01:31:52.179
They're fucking coming! Hurry!

1088
01:32:01.605 --> 01:32:02.606
Yeah.

1089
01:32:03.106 --> 01:32:04.483
But this time...

1090
01:32:04.566 --> 01:32:05.567
it's you.

1091
01:32:37.099 --> 01:32:38.183
Clover!

1092
01:32:39.017 --> 01:32:40.310
Hurry!

1093
01:32:50.195 --> 01:32:51.488
Go.

1094
01:32:52.155 --> 01:32:53.365
Go, go, go.

1095
01:33:17.931 --> 01:33:19.099
The ladder.

1096
01:33:20.475 --> 01:33:21.476
Come on!

1097
01:33:32.070 --> 01:33:33.280
There's a way up!

1098
01:33:36.200 --> 01:33:37.951
Come on, get up.

1099
01:34:06.104 --> 01:34:07.314
Clover!

1100
01:34:07.397 --> 01:34:08.982
No! No!

1101
01:34:21.870 --> 01:34:24.540
- Clover!
- We got you, we got you.

1102
01:34:27.042 --> 01:34:28.752
Megan!

1103
01:34:48.480 --> 01:34:49.481
What's happening?

1104
01:34:52.234 --> 01:34:55.153
Look. Look. The sky.

1105
01:35:14.715 --> 01:35:15.966
We did it.

1106
01:35:16.842 --> 01:35:18.218
It's over.

1107
01:35:24.349 --> 01:35:25.350
Jesus!

1108
01:35:25.434 --> 01:35:27.474
You guys planning on staying
another night, or what?
